<title>TAIWAN: Chiao Tung falls on gov't sell-off.</title>
<headline>Chiao Tung falls on gov't sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiao Tung Bank fell sharply at mid-session on Tuesday following the finance ministry's auction of some 115.5 million shares of the state-run bank on Monday.</p>
<p>After 80 minutes at 0220 GMT, Chiao Tung was down the daily seven percent limit or T$5.50 at T$74.50.</p>
<p>Monday was the first day of a scheduled five-day auction during which the ministry planned to sell off nearly 418 million shares -- which would reduce state's stake in the bank to 60.03 percent from 88.83 percent.</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
